GUI:TogglePurchaseScience
"Generals Promotions"
END

GUI:TogglePurchaseScienceDescription
"Opens and closes the general's promotion screen."
END

GUI:Stop
"Stop"
END

GUI:StopDescription
"Stops what the selected units are doing."
END

// The command grid's own attack, hold position and move keys, which stand in no command set:
// the cards they show under the pointer.

GUI:OrderForceAttack
"Force Attack"
END

GUI:OrderForceAttackDescription
"The next click attacks whatever is under the pointer, the ground and your own side included. Click the key again to call it off."
END

GUI:OrderHoldPosition
"Hold Position"
END

GUI:OrderHoldPositionDescription
"The selected units guard the spot they stand on and fight whatever comes near, without chasing it out of the area."
END

GUI:OrderMove
"Move"
END

GUI:OrderMoveDescription
"The next click on the ground sends the selected units there. Drag instead and they spread out along the line you draw."
END

GUI:OrderSearchAndDestroy
"Search and Destroy"
END

GUI:OrderSearchAndDestroyDescription
"Click a spot and the selected units attack move round it, fighting whatever they run into, then stay and guard the whole circle. Roll the mouse wheel before you click to size the circle."
END

GUI:OrderStanceDefensive
"Stance: Defensive"
END

GUI:OrderStanceDefensiveDescription
"The selected units shoot what comes into range and hold the ground you put them on. Click to make them aggressive: they go after any enemy they see."
END

GUI:OrderStanceAggressive
"Stance: Aggressive"
END

GUI:OrderStanceAggressiveDescription
"The selected units go after any enemy they see and chase it. Click to make them defensive again: they only shoot what comes into range and stay where they are."
END

// Smoke signals.  The three ...Placed lines are what an ally reads; %s is the sender's name.  The
// ...Label words are written over the smoke, which is in the sender's colour.
GUI:SignalAttack
"Signal: Attack"
END

GUI:SignalAttackDescription
"Smoke in your colour and crossed swords on the ground for ten seconds, where the cursor is or on the radar spot under it. Only your allies see it."
END

GUI:SignalDefend
"Signal: Defend"
END

GUI:SignalDefendDescription
"Smoke in your colour and a shield on the ground for ten seconds, where the cursor is or on the radar spot under it. Only your allies see it."
END

GUI:SignalAttention
"Signal: Look Here"
END

GUI:SignalAttentionDescription
"Smoke in your colour and an eye on the ground for ten seconds, where the cursor is or on the radar spot under it. Only your allies see it."
END

GUI:SignalAttackPlaced
"%s: attack here!"
END

GUI:SignalDefendPlaced
"%s: defend here!"
END

GUI:SignalAttentionPlaced
"%s: look here!"
END

GUI:TogglePause
"Pause"
END

GUI:TogglePauseDescription
"Pauses and resumes the game. Single player and replays only."
END

GUI:GamePaused
"Game paused."
END

GUI:GameResumed
"Game resumed."
END

GUI:SelectAllMilitary
"Select Military Units"
END

GUI:SelectAllMilitaryDescription
"Selects your armed units on screen. Press again to select them across the whole map."
END

GUI:SelectAllVehicles
"Select Vehicles"
END

GUI:SelectAllVehiclesDescription
"Selects your ground vehicles on screen, dozers and workers excluded. Press again for the whole map."
END

GUI:SelectAllBarracks
"Select Barracks"
END

GUI:SelectAllBarracksDescription
"Selects your infantry-producing buildings on screen. Press again to select them across the whole map."
END

GUI:SelectAllWarFactories
"Select War Factories"
END

GUI:SelectAllWarFactoriesDescription
"Selects your vehicle-producing buildings on screen. Press again to select them across the whole map."
END

GUI:SelectAllAirfields
"Select Airfields"
END

GUI:SelectAllAirfieldsDescription
"Selects your airfields and helipads on screen. Press again to select them across the whole map."
END

